  <section class="apdp-tail apdp-tail-faq apdp-shell apdp-dialfit-full alta-pdp-flow-section apdp-dialfit-section" aria-labelledby="AltaeronFaq-{{ section.id }}">
    {% render 'altaeron-pdp-section-heading', number: '10', title: 'Frequently Asked Questions', subtitle: 'Everything you need to choose and use DialFit with confidence.', heading_id: 'AltaeronFaq' %}
    <div class="apdp-tail-accordion">
      <details><summary>Is this the same knee brace shown in the video?{% render 'icon-accordion-chevron', class: 'apdp-tail-accordion__chevron' %}</summary><p>Yes. This is the Altaeron™ DialFit Knee Brace featuring the same dial-adjustment mechanism shown in our videos.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Do I need the Left or Right version?{% render 'icon-accordion-chevron', class: 'apdp-tail-accordion__chevron' %}</summary><p>Choose the side that matches the knee you plan to wear it on. DialFit has separate Left Knee and Right Knee versions.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What does the dial actually do?{% render 'icon-accordion-chevron', class: 'apdp-tail-accordion__chevron' %}</summary><p>The dial adjusts the tension around the brace, letting you fine-tune how secure and supportive it feels around your knee.</p></details>
      <details><summary>How tight should I wear it?{% render 'icon-accordion-chevron', class: 'apdp-tail-accordion__chevron' %}</summary><p>DialFit should feel snug and supportive, not painfully tight. If you experience numbness, tingling, unusual swelling or discomfort, loosen or remove it.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can I use it for running or workouts?{% render 'icon-accordion-chevron', class: 'apdp-tail-accordion__chevron' %}</summary><p>Yes. DialFit is designed for active movement such as walking, gym training, running, hiking and everyday activities.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can I wear it during a long work shift?{% render 'icon-accordion-chevron', class: 'apdp-tail-accordion__chevron' %}</summary><p>Yes. The adjustable design is useful for people who spend long periods standing or walking. You can adjust the tension as your comfort needs change throughout the day.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What if I have varicose veins?{% render 'icon-accordion-chevron', class: 'apdp-tail-accordion__chevron' %}</summary><p>DialFit is a knee-support brace, not a treatment for varicose veins. People who also experience tired or heavy legs may still use it for knee-focused support while standing or walking. For a vascular condition, follow advice from an appropriate healthcare professional.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Is it bulky?{% render 'icon-accordion-chevron', class: 'apdp-tail-accordion__chevron' %}</summary><p>No. DialFit uses a lightweight stretch construction designed to provide support without the bulk of many traditional rigid knee braces.</p></details>
      <details><summary>How do I choose my size?{% render 'icon-accordion-chevron', class: 'apdp-tail-accordion__chevron' %}</summary><p>Use the Size Guide and choose according to the manufacturer's body-weight range.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can it cure arthritis or repair a knee injury?{% render 'icon-accordion-chevron', class: 'apdp-tail-accordion__chevron' %}</summary><p>DialFit is designed to provide additional support and comfort while worn. It is not intended to repair an underlying injury or replace appropriate medical treatment.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What if it doesn't work for me?{% render 'icon-accordion-chevron', class: 'apdp-tail-accordion__chevron' %}</summary><p>You're covered by our 30-Day Money-Back Guarantee. Try DialFit during your normal routine and contact us within the guarantee period if it isn't right for you.</p></details>
    </div>
  </section>

